# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.js
.yarn/install-state.gz

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# local env files
.env*.local

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# content (should be tracked in its own repo)
/content
/test-content
/test-remotes
/test-clones

# settings (local editor configuration)
/settings
/test-settings

# playwright
/playwright-report
/test-results
/playwright/.cache
/playwright/.auth
/blob-report
/blob-reports
# The three-recipes fixture has no featured recipes; a stray featured-recipes
# LMDB index gets generated there by test runs. Ignore that spurious artifact.
/playwright/fixtures/test-content/three-recipes/featured-recipes/
# The same artifact, for groups — but as a rule rather than one fixture, because
# every fixture is copied into `test-content` and any page the run visits can
# open the groups environment there. `three-recipes-groups` is the one fixture
# whose groups are real content, so it is carved back out. Order matters: a
# negation only works if the pattern above it does not exclude the directory
# itself, which is why both lines name `groups/` and not `groups/**`.
/playwright/fixtures/test-content/*/groups/
!/playwright/fixtures/test-content/three-recipes-groups/groups/
# `three-recipes-groups` inherits the featured-recipes artifact above, and gains
# a `pages` one, because 22b's export-build check points `CONTENT_DIRECTORY`
# straight at this fixture — so the export opens every environment it reads,
# right here, rather than in a copy. Named per fixture rather than as a
# wildcard: `about-page` and `two-pages` have real `pages/` content, and
# `one-featured-recipe` real featured recipes.
/playwright/fixtures/test-content/three-recipes-groups/featured-recipes/
/playwright/fixtures/test-content/three-recipes-groups/pages/

.env
